    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>採用學期成績記分法、出席及缺席、課堂互動與參與討論、作業提交及遲交、考評及補考</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "1. After hearing the class bell, students should immediately enter the classroom and take their seats according to the number of seats.\n2. Once the seats of each student are assigned, they cannot be changed arbitrarily.\n3. When the teacher enters the classroom during the class, and when the teacher leaves the classroom when the class is over, the students should stand up and salute\nRespectfully.\n4. When the teacher raises a question and requires the student to answer it, the student should immediately stand up and respond.\n5. When students have questions and must ask the teacher, they should wait until the teacher has finished speaking before standing up to ask questions.\n6. Students do not have to stand up when there are guests visiting during class.\n7. Keep quiet during class, turn off mobile phones (including alarms), concentrate on listening to lectures, and do not fall asleep,\nChatting with neighbors, reading non-classic books, newspapers or doing other homework, let alone talking loudly\nLaughing, or other behaviors that interfere with classroom order.\n8. The walls, glass, blackboard, desks and chairs, floor, podium and desk in the classroom must be cleaned regularly\nKeep it tidy, and do not smear or throw paper scraps, peels, and dirt at will.",
    "course_pol_en": null,
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>Adhere to the principle of academic integrity in all academic works. We expect students to act with integrity when engaging in academic activities<br />\nrequirements. include:<br />\n&bull; Be responsible for all submissions;<br />\n&bull; Ensure that all work submitted is original; and<br />\n&bull; Indicate in detail and correctly the sources and intellectual property rights of the materials cited in the work.<br />\nAcademically, you should be upright and honest, and you should refrain from any inappropriate behavior that affects your personal future and the reputation of the University. The following will tell<br />\nThe importance of your integrity and honesty is good for your academic development. If you have any questions or inquiries, please seek guidance and assistance from staff<br />\nhelp.</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": null,
